      "postID": "6090b4a0da8a7b574b4994b5",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've found some what of a work around till VrChat looks at how their systems work:\nWalk away from the spawn point. Usually the further the better. Change into another avatar and calibrate. Change back into the one you was using and calibrate. The leg isn't perfect, but it'll animate better. If this was our rig, both legs would do it, or hell, the whole hip would break. This is som'in that the game is doing. It's improperly reading the right foot's tracking. The arm twist thing though? I dono. My models don't do it but have seen it in action.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
